   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "That means core loss vanishes, so the wattmeter measures pure full-load copper loss.",
    "imageQuery": "digital power analyzer",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "compare",
     "caption": "Losses in SC Test",
     "items": [
      {
       "label": "Core Loss",
       "symbol": "❌"
      },
      {
       "label": "Copper Loss",
       "symbol": "🔥"
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Recall that electric power dissipated as heat in a resistor equals current squared times resistance.",
    "imageQuery": "engineering textbook formula",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "P{sc} = I{sc}^2 \\times R{eq}",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Rearranging this basic relation gives resistance as power divided by current squared directly.",
    "imageQuery": "whiteboard derivation",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "R{eq} = P{sc} / I{sc}^2",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Substituting two hundred watts divided by twenty amperes squared gives two hundred over four hundred.",
    "imageQuery": "calculator display closeup",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "R{eq} = 200 / (20^2) = 200 / 400",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Two hundred divided by four hundred simplifies straight away to zero point five ohms.",
    "imageQuery": "engineering calculation sheet",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "icon",
     "caption": "Calculated Req",
     "items": [
      {
       "label": "0.5 Ω",
       "symbol": "✅"
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "kind": "explain",
    "narration": "Dividing voltage by current would give total impedance, which is one point five ohms instead.",
    "imageQuery": "oscilloscope screen trace",
    "visual": {
     "kind": "formula",
     "formula": "Z{eq} = 30V / 20A = 1.5\\,\\Omega",
     "caption": ""
    }
   },
